  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nThe 5h ridge will remain in place across the southern U.S. next \nweek, with west-northwest flow across the central Plains into the \nOH and TN valleys. The question is how amplified and it's eastward\ninfluence into the TN Valley and southeast U.S. The ECMWF is a \nbit more amplified with the ridge in the Rockies and Plains which \ncould inflate convective chances and some heat relief at times due\nto a more northwesterly flow if this verifies. For now, forecast \nhighs in the middle to upper 90s on Monday may drop into the lower\nto middle 90s in valley areas Tuesday through Thursday (upper 80s\nto around 90 atop the higher Cumberland Plateau areas). Overnight\nlows in the middle to upper 70s will dip into lower to middle \n70s. For now, PoPs remain low on a day to day basis next week, but\nthis certainly could waiver upward depending on the evolution of \nthe ridge and northwesterly flow/MCS cluster tracks around the \nperiphery of the ridge.",
